                <pb facs="0832" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg666"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-24T11:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1916, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>325. Your 153, August 22, 5 p.m. Foreign Minister informs me in writing as
                    follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Danish Government has not understood the clause in question as
                            imposing upon the Government of the United States any engagement to
                            assist in the <pb facs="0833" n="667" xml:id="pg667"/> maintenance of
                            the churches and church property by appropriations for the maintenance,
                            repairs and salaries of clergymen or to act as trustee for the religious
                            associations or corporations concerned.—<hi rendition="#small-caps">Erik
                                Scavenius.</hi>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Egan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
